# Release Checklist

Run top to bottom. No step is optional. The app is one codebase behind a
service worker, so a skipped step ships a stale or broken build to real users.

## 1. Pre-flight
- [ ] Working tree is clean (`git status`).
- [ ] On a branch named for the change, not `main`.
- [ ] Data backed up: Sync → Pull on the laptop, or Tools → Export JSON.
      A failed pull means STOP — export instead.

## 2. Bump the build
- [ ] `app.js`: `var BUILD="vN"` incremented.
- [ ] `sw.js`: `const C="stack-vN"` matches the same number.
- [ ] Mismatched numbers are the #1 cause of stale-HTML bugs. They must agree.

## 3. Smoke test (local, before push)
- [ ] All 5 nav tabs load: Today, Calendar, Body, Sites, More.
- [ ] Calendar: current month renders, Prev/Next work, tapping a past day
      expands it with Edit buttons.
- [ ] Dose math: open a compound with a set concentration, confirm units and
      mL both display and match `mg / mgPerMl * 100`.
- [ ] PRN: Propranolol and Viagra appear under As needed, not Medications.
- [ ] Med check-off works on Today and on a past Calendar day.
- [ ] Gist round-trip: Push, then Pull, confirm data returns intact.
- [ ] Export produces a file; Import of that file restores it.
- [ ] Pause a compound, confirm past logged days still show it.

## 4. Deploy
- [ ] Commit with a message naming what changed and what was verified.
- [ ] Push.
- [ ] On the phone: Tools → Force refresh, then close and reopen the app.
- [ ] Confirm the header/Build string shows the new version.

## 5. Post-deploy
- [ ] Open Calendar, confirm it is still the second nav slot.
- [ ] Log one throwaway dose, confirm inventory decrements, then undo it and
      confirm inventory returns.
- [ ] Tag the release (`git tag vN`).

## Rollback
- Revert the commit, bump BUILD and C to a fresh number, push, Force refresh.
- If data is corrupted, Pull the last good gist or Import the last export.
